=== sg_inq ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Performs a SCSI INQUIRY command on DEVICE or decodes INQUIRY response held
in file FN. If no options given then does a 'standard' INQUIRY. Can list VPD
pages with '--vpd' or '--page=PG' option. The sg_vpd and sdparm utilities
decode more VPD pages than this utility.


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  sg_inq [--block=0|1] [--cmddt] [--descriptors] [--export] [--extended]
      [--help] [--hex] [--id] [--inhex=FN] [--len=LEN] [--long]
      [--maxlen=LEN] [--only] [--page=PG] [--raw] [--verbose] [--version]
      [--vpd] DEVICE


POSITIONALS (1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  DEVICE


FLAGS (22) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Where
    --block={…}  0-> open(non-blocking); 1-> open(blocking)
                   values: 0, 1
-B {…}           (def: depends on OS; Linux pt: 0)
                   values: 0, 1
-c, --cmddt      command support data mode (set opcode with '--page=PG') use
                 twice for list of supported commands; obsolete
-d, --descriptors fetch and decode version descriptors
-u, --export     SCSI_IDENT_<assoc>_<type>=<ident> output format. Defaults
                 to device id page (0x83) if --page not given, only
                 supported for VPD pages 0x80 and 0x83
-E, --extended   decode extended INQUIRY data VPD page (0x86)
 or -x
-f, --force      skip VPD page 0 check; directly fetch requested page
-h, --help       print usage message then exit
-H, --hex        output response in hex
-i, --id         decode device identification VPD page (0x83)
-I, --inhex=FN   read ASCII hex from file FN instead of DEVICE; if used with
                 --raw then read binary from FN
-l, --len=LEN    requested response length (def: 0 -> fetch 36 bytes first,
                 then fetch again as indicated)
-L, --long       supply extra information on NVMe devices
-m, --maxlen=LEN same as '--len='
-O, --old        use old interface (use as first option)
-o, --only       for std inquiry do not fetch serial number vpd page; for
                 NVMe device only do Identify controller
-p, --page=PG    Vital Product Data (VPD) page number or abbreviation
                 (opcode number if '--cmddt' given)
-r, --raw        output response in binary (to stdout)
-s, --vendor     show vendor specific fields in std inquiry
-v, --verbose    increase verbosity
-V, --version    print version string then exit
-e, --vpd        vital product data (set page with '--page=PG')
